{{DISPLAYTITLE:<span style="color: #888888;">Giant Snowball</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=2|Rarity=Common|Type=Spell|Arena=Frozen Peak|ReleaseDate=20 June 2018}}{{SubpageNavBox|Evolution=yes}}{{Quote|It’s HUGE! Once it began rolling down Frozen Peak, there was no stopping it. Enemies hit are knocked back and slowed down. Reduced damage to Crown Towers.}}

The Giant Snowball is a {{Rarity|Common}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from [[Arenas|Frozen Peak (Arena 8)]]. It is an area-damage, air-targeting [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] with a medium radius and low damage. When used, it slows enemies in its radius for 3 seconds and inflict knockback. It is an oversized snowball. A Giant Snowball card costs 2 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Modifiers==
===[[File:Giant Snowball Common Modifier.png|45x45px]] Common: Practically Glacial===
{{Quote|+300% slow duration}}
Giant Snowball's duration is increased by 300%, for a total of 12 seconds.

===[[File:Giant Snowball Rare Modifier.png|45x45px]] Rare: Get Outta Here!===
{{Quote|+300% knockback}}
Giant Snowball's pushback range is increased by 300%, for a total of 6 tiles.

===[[File:Giant Snowball Epic Modifier.png|45x45px]] Epic: Snowball Fight!===
{{Quote|5 Evo Snowballs}}
Instead of a Giant Snowball, 5 Evolved Giant Snowballs are launched.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Giant Snowball Card}}
*The Giant Snowball is a 2 [[Elixir]] utility [[Cards|card]] that is an effective finisher against [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] with low hitpoints.
*This card excels at disrupting enemy pushes by knocking them back and slowing them down briefly, giving the defending player extra time to attack or defend. Its knockback effect can reset an [[Inferno Dragon]]'s ramp up attack or a [[Battle Ram]], Ram Rider, and [[Royal Recruits/Evolution|Evolved Royal Recruits]]' charge. However, this is not to be confused with a stun, as the Giant Snowball will not reset an [[Inferno Tower]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Prince]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Mega Knight]], or a [[Sparky]].
*Its knockback effect is the same as that of [[Fireball]]; it is a true stun that resets the attack animations of small to medium sized troops. This is in contrast to a normal stun such as that of the [[Zap]], which stalls attack animations but does not reset them.
*The Giant Snowball can activate the [[King's Tower]] with a poorly placed [[Miner]] or [[Goblin Barrel]]. The Miner activation only works if the opponent plays their Miner on the corner of the [[:Category:Tower Troop Cards|Crown Tower]] that is closest to the King.
*A Goblin Barrel can be easily defeated with large swarm cards like a [[Skeleton Army]] or a [[Goblin Gang|Goblin Gang.]] A Giant Snowball can prevent them from surrounding the [[Goblins]] spawned from the Goblin Barrel, allowing them to connect to the Crown Tower instead, but it doesn't mitigate their weakness to such [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] such as [[The Log]] or [[Arrows]].
*Since it can be deployed anywhere in the [[Arenas|Arena]] and moves decently fast, the Giant Snowball can force a troop close to the center of the Arena to switch lanes, possibly hampering the opponent's future plays.
*The Giant Snowball has the ability to mitigate a majority of stray damage from frail, lone support troops like a [[Musketeer]] or a [[Wizard]] for a positive Elixir trade, in some cases even preventing the damage entirely. Time the Snowball so that it lands right as the enemy troop is about to attack to reduce the damage taken as much as possible.
*The Giant Snowball's knockback mechanic can be used to force enemy troops into favorable positions for the defender. For example, the knockback can force a [[Hog Rider]] off the player's Crown Tower and onto a defensive [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] like the [[Cannon]], [[Tesla]], [[X-Bow]], [[Bomb Tower]], or [[Mortar]].
*With proper timing, the Giant Snowball can also be an effective support on offense, destroying low hitpoint troops and knocking back and slowing down other incoming troops.
*The Giant Snowball works fairly well with the [[Ram Rider]]. On offense, the spell can knock defenders away from the player's Ram Rider while she simultaneously snares them, leaving them nearly immobile for several seconds and will allow the Ram Rider to deal much more damage. It also weakens low-health troops enough for the Ram Rider to finish them off with her snare attack. On defense, the Ram Rider will snare and slow down enemy troops, and Giant Snowball will push them back (if small or medium sized) and slow them even more, making it extremely difficult for slow moving troops like a [[Balloon]], [[Giant]], Sparky, [[Elixir Golem]], P.E.K.K.A, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Skeleton King]], Mighty Miner, [[Battle Healer]], or [[Golem]] to connect.
**Conversely, Giant Snowball is also a fairly reliable counter to the Ram Rider. Time the Giant Snowball such that it knocks the Ram Rider backwards just as her charge is about to connect to the Crown Tower to reset her charge and reduce tower damage.
*Another good synergy is with [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]]. It can knock an [[Ice Golem]] further away from the P.E.K.K.A to prevent her being kited to the other lane. This requires precise timing and some degree of prediction, however.
*The Giant Snowball is comparable to the Zap. The Giant Snowball offers a large knockback and long slowdown, while the Zap also has instant damage, slightly higher damage, and a stun to reset enemy charges. Zap however, cannot fully counter a Goblin Barrel.
*Similarly, The Giant Snowball is comparable to the [[Rage]]. The Giant Snowball offers a large knockback and long slowdown, while the Rage can use its damage quicker on offense, has slightly higher damage, and can be used boost the attack and movement speed troops. Rage however, cannot fully counter a Goblin Barrel.
**This means a prediction Snowball on offense is often more effective than a prediction Zap would be, as the travel time of the Snowball is much less relevant in this scenario.
**This means the Giant Snowball is often the more effective spell over Rage on defense while the Rage is the more effective spell on offense.
**Since the Snowball deals knockback and has a circular area of effect, it is harder to use with Fireball as the knockback from one spell may cause the other to miss. The player should make sure to have both of them in hand, and deploy each one of them long after the other one hits its intended target.
**It is better at keeping troops inside a [[Poison]] than Zap is, thanks to the knockback and slow effect.
*When placed correctly, a Giant Snowball can fully counter a lone center placed Goblin Barrel. The player should hover their Snowball over the Crown Tower and deploy it when the shadow of the Goblin Barrel is 0-2 tiles above the Crown Tower.
*With the help of the [[Dart Goblin]], the Giant Snowball can fully counter the [[Wall Breakers/Evolution|Evolved Wall Breakers]]. Although this is a -2 trade, the Dart Goblin will counterattack if left ignored, dealing a large amount of chip damage.
**Conversely, the Giant Snowball can fully counter an offensive Dart Goblin when timed and placed properly.

